# A0 optimizer, written in A0 (DESIGN.md 7a): the port of src/optimize.ts `optimizeFunction`
# (readThroughFills, expand, pass, forwardAggregates, schedule, literal iterations), node for
# node what the TypeScript optimizer gives: same nodes in the same order, same operands, same
# ret, tools/selfhost-wasm.ts `a0IrCheck` compares them (and the literal iteration bound) on
# every function.
#
# One run optimizes ONE function (`ozone`, mode 7 of `emitwasmio`): a single A0 value, a fold
# state included, is at most 65536 words, and a function's operand table alone can fill that, so
# no run can hold a loop over functions. The driver runs the functions of a program in program
# order and feeds each run the optimized bodies it needs (src/optimize.ts `optimizedCallee`: an
# optimized body is a function of the callee's original body and its callees' optimized
# bodies). The driver only does bookkeeping: encoding, ordering, supplying requested bodies.
#
# Input words after the mode, in the layout of the checked tables of mode 2 (paged u32x128xN;
# word w at page w>>7): types (count, triples), tlist, functions (count, 7 words each: word 0
# is bit 0 "has a body" and literalIterations * 2, 1 the parameter count, 2 the first
# parameter in tlist, 3 the result type, 4 the first node, 5 the node count, 6 the packed ret
# kind * 2^28 + value, kind 5: the pair at operand slot value), nodes (count, 6 words each: 0,
# op, operand count, first operand slot, callee, predicate; callee and predicate are function
# indices), the node types, operand pairs (count, kind and value, kinds 1 node 2 parameter 3
# u32 4 bool), then for every function two summary words (node count; bit 0 all parameters
# scalar, 1 result scalar, 2 all node types scalar, 3 some type holds io, 4 every type at most
# 64 words), the index of the function to optimize (its original body; every other function
# has a body only when the run needs it) and a stage (0; 1.. stops after a phase, for the
# comparison with the TypeScript phases). Output words with code 0: the node count, per node
# op, operand count, callee, predicate, type, the operand pairs (node references renumbered to
# positions), then the ret pair and the literal iteration bound. Code 7: the functions whose
# body the run needs (to inline a call or unroll a fold, or to evaluate a call or a fold with
# literal operands, on the optimized body as src/optimize.ts does), then their count; the driver
# supplies them and everything they reach and repeats the run. Public modes 7/8 give code 5
# and write nothing on supplied checked ops. Strict metadata is not part of the table ABI.
# Code 4: a limit (4096 nodes,
# 32768 operand slots, 256 stacked nodes) was reached; src/optimize.ts has none of these.
#
# The work is a sequence of phases on separate tables, since no state can hold them all:
# arena node table CL (a column per field, node ids are arena indices, AN = 4096), sequence SQ of
# the body's nodes, operand pairs OA (the input operand table, rewritten in place; new operand
# lists are appended after the input's), type facts TI. A phase decides (a fold over the nodes
# whose state is a table of per-node columns, one trip a node, each step a fold of 0 or 1 trips
# so that no function is larger than the chunk limits) and then materializes (one fold a
# table). Table reads are written out inline in the steps (a table passed to a call is copied by
# the C emitter); the macros `rdp`, `karg`, ... are expanded here by the generator.
#
# - expand (`edstep`): weighted-cost pure scalar calls are inlined and folds of 1..8
#   literal trips unrolled (ordinary nodes cost 1, call/fold/loop cost 5; thresholds 16,
#   256 per body and 2048 total). Square-matrix recurrences are powered first when cheaper.
#   Both fold rewrites require no io and at most 64 words a result/node type. Rename table
#   RN, output sequence and instances describe copied or synthesized nodes.
# - pass (`passa`..`passd`): per node, in order, operands resolved through the substitutions;
#   a variable trip count that propagation would make a literal beyond the static compute bound
#   (2^24 trips times the callee's literal iterations) is kept as a `mov` of that literal;
#   effectful nodes (read write puts; call fold loop holding io) are kept and anchored;
#   constant evaluation (the evaluator of compiler/evalrun.a0, on the optimized bodies, fuel as
#   src/core.ts);
#   algebraic identities; reassociation of literal chains; strength reduction (div and rem by a
#   power of two); common-subexpression elimination (hash table, not arr rec; commutative ops
#   as a multiset); dead-code elimination from the ret and the anchored nodes.
# - readThroughFills (`rtda`..`rtds`) before expand, and in each of up to eight more rounds
#   (else forwardAggregates, `fwda`..`fwdo`), each followed by a pass while it changes something.
# - schedule (`schstep`): the demand-driven order when nothing is effectful and no set/put
#   remains; literal iterations (`listep`); output (`ozwnode`).
#
# The evaluator (compiler/evalrun.a0; src/core.ts `exec`) is a machine with an explicit frame stack: `evstep`,
# charging 1 per function entry, 1 per node, 1 per fold/loop trip inside a body and
# max(1, length) for arr rec text set put; a call with literal operands runs on fuel 4096 (its
# exhaustion is a compile error in TypeScript: code 4), a fold/loop with at most 4096 trips on
# fuel 4096 * 64 (exhaustion keeps the node).
#
# `ozopt1` is the same optimizer as a function of the tables of a chunk, for compiler/shape.a0
# (the fused bodies it appends are optimized as src/optimize.ts `finishBody` does): see its
# comment below; mode 8 of `emitwasmio` runs it on the input of mode 7 (without the summaries
# and the stage; it computes the summaries itself and asks for every callee body).
#
# Known differences from src/optimize.ts: the limits above, and the evaluator's capacities
# (1024 frames, 16368 environment words, 40832 heap words): a call that exhausts them is code
# 4, a fold that does so is kept as a loop, where TypeScript has no capacity.
#
# compiler/optimize.a0 is generated from compiler/optimize.a0s by tools/a0s.ts (an expression
# language that compiles to one-node-per-line A0; see its header): edit the source, not this
# file.

use "evalrun.a0"

